            <h2>History of Bhutan</h2>
            <p>Bhutan has a recorded history dating back to the 7th century with the establishment of Buddhism by Guru Rinpoche. It maintained independence through careful diplomacy, balancing relations with neighboring India and China. Bhutan was unified as a nation under the Wangchuck dynasty in the early 20th century and transitioned to democracy in 2008, all the while preserving its unique cultural heritage and environment.</p>
